Consider your lowest card in relation to the last_played_card. If your card is very close to the last_played_card, you should wait less. If it's significantly higher, you should wait more, allowing lower cards from other players to be played first. Remember, your wait time is your only signal.

Your chosen wait time communicates information to your teammates. A short wait suggests you have a low card ready to play soon. A long wait suggests your lowest card is relatively high, giving others with lower cards time to play.

The num_other_cards indicates how many cards are still in play among your teammates. If this number is high, there's a greater chance someone else has a lower card than yours, so you might need to wait longer. If it's low, you might need to be quicker.

